Senator Imee R. Marcos: time, propose the following

asr-000104
00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:44.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: questions. Under Section

asr-000105
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 2 of RA

asr-000106
00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: No. 11059,

asr-000107
00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:49.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: the Ombudsman, the Deputy Ombudsman,

asr-000108
00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: the Special Prosecutor

asr-000109
00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: are generally required

asr-000110
00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: to serve their full

asr-000111
00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:56.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: seven-term,

asr-000112
00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: seven-year term

asr-000113
00:17:59.560 --> 00:17:59.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: to qualify

asr-000114
00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: for the retirement benefits

asr-000115
00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: prescribed therein.

asr-000116
00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is that correct, Mr. Chair?

asr-000117
00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:07.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Section 2.

asr-000118
00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, that's correct.

asr-000119
00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:12.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: However, under the Special Provision No. 6

asr-000120
00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:16.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: of the OMB's Appropriations in 2026

asr-000121
00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: last year's budget,

asr-000122
00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: proposed again in the amendments

asr-000123
00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:24.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: for GAA 2027,

asr-000124
00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: under the Senate version

asr-000125
00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:28.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: of the 2027 GAB,

asr-000126
00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:29.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: proposed again in the amendments for GAA 2027, under the Senate version of the 2027 GAB,

asr-000127
00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:30.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: proposed again in the amendments for GAA 2027, under the Senate version of the 2027 GAB,

asr-000128
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:35.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: these officials may qualify for the same retirement benefits

asr-000129
00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:40.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: after serving a mere two years in their respective positions,

asr-000130
00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:44.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: provided that they have rendered at least seven years of government service.

asr-000131
00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:52.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Please refer to the special provision number six of the OMB appropriations.

asr-000132
00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:59.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It occurs in 2026 as well as the GAB of 2027.

asr-000133
00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:05.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is this not in effect an amendment to RA 11059?

asr-000134
00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:11.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: No, it's not an amendment according to RO Bootsman.

asr-000135
00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:20.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I believe it's an amendment very clearly because the requirement of the special law

asr-000136
00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:27.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: is that the entire full seven-year term should first be served

asr-000137
00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: in order to qualify for the retirement.

asr-000138
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:38.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Suddenly, a mere two years will be adequate for full retirement benefits.

asr-000139
00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:44.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: This is a complete and drastic change and effectively amends the special law.

asr-000140
00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It should be noted.

asr-000141
00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:56.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-000142
00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:56.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-000143
00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:08.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It should be noted.

asr-000144
00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:12.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, this provision was recommended by the Ombudsman.

asr-000145
00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:20.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Office of Ombudsman will have the chance or the opportunity to be able to recruit

asr-000146
00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:26.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: new blood, young blood, fresh blood with courage, integrity, and determination

asr-000147
00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to continue its fight.

asr-000148
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Against corruption, no?

asr-000149
00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:46.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We do not want to belittle the former officers who were appointed in those positions.

asr-000150
00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:56.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But I guess in this time, it's a different ballgame right now, especially with the recent biggest corruption in history.

asr-000151
00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:59.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Office of the Ombudsman has never been...

asr-000152
00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It's been more active and dynamic.

asr-000153
00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:12.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So they would want to recruit younger, fresh blood, again, with the courage and integrity

asr-000154
00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:15.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to fight graft and corruption.

asr-000155
00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:21.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, I applaud that purpose, and we all recognize the present conditions.

asr-000156
00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:28.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: However, what would be the proper measure would be to amend RA 11059,

asr-000157
00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:33.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and not do it indirectly through a general law like the GAA.

asr-000158
00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:39.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It should be noted that Article 6 in Section 25.2 of the Constitution

asr-000159
00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:45.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: expressly limits the scope and operation of special provisions in the GAA.

asr-000160
00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:48.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It's very, very clear in the Constitution.

asr-000161
00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:56.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So what is the constitutional basis for modifying statutory qualifications for retirement benefits

asr-000162
00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:58.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: through an annual appropriations?

asr-000163
00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:00.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: This law, this is not on.

asr-000164
00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:06.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Your Honor, the special provision does not amend the Constitution,

asr-000165
00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:12.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: particularly the Section 11 of Article 11 that was mentioned.

asr-000166
00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:18.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It applies only to the calculation of the number of years of service for the Ombudsman,

asr-000167
00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:24.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the Deputy Ombudsman, or Special Prosecutor to be eligible for retirement benefits

asr-000168
00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:27.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: under Republic Act 1105,

asr-000169
00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:28.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: which is the...

asr-000170
00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:30.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the Retirement Law of the Office of the Ombudsman.

asr-000171
00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:34.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It does not seek to amend the seven-year term limit for the Ombudsman

asr-000172
00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:37.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: under the 1987 Constitution.

asr-000173
00:22:38.320 --> 00:22:41.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: No, we understand that the provision only applies to the Ombudsman,

asr-000174
00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:44.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: the Deputy Ombudsman, and the Special Prosecutors,

asr-000175
00:22:45.060 --> 00:22:46.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and not to the others,

asr-000176
00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:49.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: which arguably makes it worse because it's preferential.

asr-000177
00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:52.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the question will arise,

asr-000178
00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:54.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: is Boeing intending to retire?

asr-000179
00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:55.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I think not.

asr-000180
00:22:55.820 --> 00:22:58.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, why was this proposed?

asr-000181
00:22:58.440 --> 00:22:59.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why was this proposed?

asr-000182
00:22:59.320 --> 00:23:05.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I think I would like to cite also the case of Pimentel III v. the House of Representatives,

asr-000183
00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:10.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: decided very recently, as a matter of fact, on the 3rd of December 2025.

asr-000184
00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:17.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the Supreme Court reiterated this absolute prohibition against amending substantive laws

asr-000185
00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:19.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: through the GAA.

asr-000186
00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:23.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: How can we reconcile the special provision with this ruling?

asr-000187
00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:23.600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

asr-000188
00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:27.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi po pwede yan eh.

asr-000189
00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:27.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi,

asr-000190
00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: andyan yung konstitusyon,

asr-000191
00:23:29.860 --> 00:23:32.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ang liwa-liwanag ng Pimentel v. House.

asr-000192
00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:36.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, talagang alam na natin na hindi po pwede yun.

asr-000193
00:23:38.840 --> 00:23:40.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang dapat nangyari dyan,

asr-000194
00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:44.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ay dapat humingi tayo ng amendment,

asr-000195
00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:46.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: tayo naman dito sa Senado,

asr-000196
00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:49.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: very open naman tayo na i-amend na lang ang batas

asr-000197
00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:51.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: through separate legislation

asr-000198
00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:54.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: para walang duda, walang tanong,

asr-000199
00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:56.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: instead of a special provision

asr-000200
00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:57.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na parang pinalusot lamang.

asr-000201
00:23:57.880 --> 00:24:00.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sa ating GAA,

asr-000202
00:24:00.240 --> 00:24:04.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: which is a general law that cannot amend a specific or special law.

asr-000203
00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:06.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Your Honor, Mr. President,

asr-000204
00:24:06.760 --> 00:24:09.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we'd like to request for a minute's suspension.

asr-000205
00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:11.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We'll just check the Supreme Court decision

asr-000206
00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:13.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to be sure about this

asr-000207
00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:16.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: on the Pimentel v. the House of Representatives.

asr-000208
00:24:18.480 --> 00:24:20.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. President, so just a minute.

asr-000209
00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:21.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We'll just have to check.

asr-000210
00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:24.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, let me, before we suspend,

asr-000211
00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:26.880
