02:22:30.360 --> 02:22:31.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Senator Riza.

asr-002038
02:22:31.800 --> 02:22:32.180
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

asr-002039
02:22:32.780 --> 02:22:33.480
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Majority Leader.

asr-002040
02:22:36.260 --> 02:22:39.920
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, with that, we have no other members who wish to interpolate.

asr-002041
02:22:40.000 --> 02:22:46.160
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: We also got the message from the Minority Floor Leader that they will no longer interpolate the budget of the DOJ.

asr-002042
02:22:46.380 --> 02:22:54.080
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Therefore, I move, Mr. President, that the budget of the Department of Justice, Office of the Secretary, Bureau of Corrections,

asr-002043
02:22:54.520 --> 02:23:00.260
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Bureau of Immigrations, Land Registration Authority, National Bureau of Investigations,

asr-002044
02:23:00.900 --> 02:23:04.960
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Office of Alternative Dispute Resolution, Office of the Government Corporate Council,

asr-002045
02:23:05.720 --> 02:23:10.160
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Office of the Solicitor General, Parole and Probation Administration,

asr-002046
02:23:11.240 --> 02:23:15.640
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Presidential Commission on Good Government, and Public Attorney's Office be deemed submitted.

asr-002047
02:23:15.800 --> 02:23:16.700
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I so move, Mr. President.

asr-002048
02:23:16.700 --> 02:23:17.440
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Any objection?

asr-002049
02:23:18.400 --> 02:23:23.880
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hearing none, the budget of the Department of Justice and the attached agencies,

asr-002050
02:23:24.040 --> 02:23:24.500
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: and mentioned.

asr-002051
02:23:24.740 --> 02:23:28.200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: The agency's budget is hereby deemed submitted.

asr-002052
02:23:29.100 --> 02:23:30.320
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Congratulations to them.

asr-002053
02:23:30.340 --> 02:23:30.620
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

asr-002054
02:23:30.960 --> 02:23:32.140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May I ask for a minute's suspension?

asr-002055
02:23:32.360 --> 02:23:33.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Session suspended.

asr-002089
02:28:54.520 --> 02:29:04.040
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, today we will have the hard-working men and women of the Department of Agrarian Reform

asr-002090
02:29:04.040 --> 02:29:09.020
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: headed by no other than the legendary Secretary Conrad Estrella.

asr-002091
02:29:11.880 --> 02:29:13.740
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Legendary Secretary.

asr-002092
02:29:14.460 --> 02:29:20.960
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Our dear friend, dear friend of the Senate President Pro Temp, dear friend of mine and my father's, Mr. President,

asr-002093
02:29:20.960 --> 02:29:24.500
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I just want to put on record that they've been doing a great job.

asr-002094
02:29:24.520 --> 02:29:31.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: On their mandate in the Department of Agrarian Reform, one of our hard-working departments,

asr-002095
02:29:31.960 --> 02:29:41.140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and continuously, continuously performing their duties in land transfers to the people in need.

asr-002096
02:29:41.600 --> 02:29:44.760
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So, Mr. President, I move that we take up their budget.

asr-002097
02:29:45.300 --> 02:29:47.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Any objection?

asr-002098
02:29:48.260 --> 02:29:52.620
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hearing none, the budget of the Department of Agrarian Reform is hereby considered.

asr-002099
02:29:52.620 --> 02:29:53.820
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May we recognize that...

asr-002100
02:29:54.520 --> 02:29:59.640
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: ...equally hard-working chairperson of the subcommittee.

asr-002101
02:30:00.000 --> 02:30:04.620
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: No other than Senator Kiko Pangilinan, our resident agriculturist, Mr. President.

asr-002102
02:30:05.020 --> 02:30:08.800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: My favorite nephew-in-law is recognized, Senator Pangilinan.

asr-002103
02:30:08.800 --> 02:30:12.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Majority Leader.

asr-002104
02:30:13.380 --> 02:30:27.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ginoong Pangulo, sinusuportahan po natin ang panukalang budget ng Department of Agrarian Reform para sa 2027 na nagkakahalagang P16,121,735,000.

asr-002105
02:30:27.120 --> 02:30:36.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang kabuhang pondo ng DAR, Puhunan sa Siguridad sa Lupa, Kabuhayan at Katatagan ng ating mga magsasaka.

asr-002106
02:30:37.760 --> 02:30:44.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dinagdagan natin ng P1,700,000,000 sa bersyong ipinasa ng Kamara.

asr-002107
02:30:44.620 --> 02:30:54.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kabilang dito ang P600,000,000 para sa Value Chain Information for Sustainable Transformation in Agrarian Reform Communities o VISTA.

asr-002108
02:30:54.680 --> 02:30:57.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kabilang din ang P500,000,000.

asr-002109
02:30:57.120 --> 02:31:05.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: P500,000,000 bilang compensation sa mga may-ari ng lupa na saklaw ng reformang agraryo.

asr-002110
02:31:06.140 --> 02:31:15.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: VISTA is a six-year initiative from 2025 to 2030 designed to improve the livelihoods of agrarian reform beneficiaries, ARBs,

asr-002111
02:31:16.180 --> 02:31:21.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: through sustainable agriculture, enterprise development, and rural infrastructure.

asr-002112
02:31:21.200 --> 02:31:26.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: May pagkahawig sa ating sagipsaka pero nakatutok sa 70,000 small...

asr-002113
02:31:27.120 --> 02:31:31.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ...holder households sa mahigit 80 agrarian reform communities.

asr-002114
02:31:31.580 --> 02:31:40.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sa harap ng banta ng matinding El Niño, kasama rin sa VISTA ang paghahanda sa ating mga komunidad bago matuyo ang lupa.

asr-002115
02:31:40.840 --> 02:31:48.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Palalakasin nito ang supply ng tubig, rainwater collection, agroforestry, at iba pang pamamaraan ng climate adaptation.

asr-002116
02:31:50.000 --> 02:31:56.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kasabay ng mga ito, papabilisin din ng pamamahagi ng lupa at palalakasin ang serbisyong legal...

asr-002117
02:31:56.520 --> 02:31:57.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ... para makapag-aaral sa lupa.

asr-002118
02:31:57.120 --> 02:32:04.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang mga makinabang ang dapat makinabang, hindi ang mga makapangyarihang interes, kundi ang ating mga magsasaka.

asr-002119
02:32:04.880 --> 02:32:12.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Mr. President, it is also my honor to defend the agrarian reform department budget,

asr-002120
02:32:13.400 --> 02:32:21.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: considering that the Secretary is my schoolmate from the legendary LaSalle Green Hills.

asr-002121
02:32:22.700 --> 02:32:24.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Animal LaSalle.

asr-002122
02:32:24.040 --> 02:32:27.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At handa na po tayong...

asr-002123
02:32:27.120 --> 02:32:32.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ... tumugon sa mga tanong ng ating butihing mga senador. Maraming salamat po.

asr-002124
02:32:35.560 --> 02:32:38.260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Majority Leader, Sen. Amy Marcos is recognized.

asr-002125
02:32:39.000 --> 02:32:42.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, thank you very much, Mr. President, Majority Leader, our Chairman.

asr-002126
02:32:44.040 --> 02:32:53.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I simply want an update. As a long-standing agrarian reform advocate, I simply would like an update on the progress.

asr-002127
02:32:53.860 --> 02:32:56.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We have reported time and again that the number of beneficiaries...

asr-002128
02:32:57.120 --> 02:33:04.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ... from the condonation effort in 2023 was at 620,255 ARBs.

asr-002129
02:33:05.320 --> 02:33:07.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ilan na ba ngayon at ilan pa ba ang pending?

asr-002130
02:33:08.740 --> 02:33:15.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi ang alam ko, may balance pa rin tayo dun sa 57.76 billion na target natin.

asr-002131
02:33:16.140 --> 02:33:20.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Parang kulang-kulang pa ng 3 billion worth. Tama ba yun?

asr-002132
02:33:20.040 --> 02:33:24.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At ano ang plano natin para matapos na yan?

asr-002133
02:33:27.120 --> 02:33:35.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: According to the Secretary, ang nakitira na namang ay ang nasa BARM.

asr-002134
02:33:35.560 --> 02:33:36.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dahil hinihintay pa nila.

asr-002135
02:33:39.400 --> 02:33:42.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ahinintay lang nila yung eleksyon. At since tapos na...

asr-002136
02:33:42.420 --> 02:33:43.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos na.

asr-002137
02:33:45.240 --> 02:33:53.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung buong 3 billion, lahat BARM yun. Malaki-laki to ha. 283,387 hectares. Lahat yan BARM?

asr-002138
02:33:53.480 --> 02:33:55.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That is correct, according to the Secretary.

asr-002139
02:33:55.900 --> 02:33:57.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That entire balance.

asr-002140
02:33:57.120 --> 02:34:05.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So we are awaiting BARM. And we look forward to the completion of this program.

asr-002141
02:34:05.960 --> 02:34:10.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So yun yung update, yung isa pang update sana, yung tungkol sa VISTA project.

asr-002142
02:34:11.340 --> 02:34:18.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung VISTA project, yung Senate, through the Chair, restored the 600 million reduction of the House.

asr-002143
02:34:18.700 --> 02:34:23.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ayan. Eto na yung mga foreign assistant projects na binabas bawatan.

asr-002144
02:34:23.900 --> 02:34:27.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Para lang maintindihan natin at bakit rin restore ng House.

asr-002145
02:34:27.120 --> 02:34:34.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What is the purpose of the project? It's a distinction from other existing livelihood and support projects.

asr-002146
02:34:34.980 --> 02:34:37.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ano yung kanyang pakay?

asr-002147
02:34:41.340 --> 02:34:52.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actually, the VISTA, Value Chain Innovation for Sustainable Transformation in Agrarian Reform, precisely addresses the challenges of the supply chain.

asr-002148
02:34:52.920 --> 02:34:53.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oo nga.

asr-002149
02:34:53.400 --> 02:34:56.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dahil pag buhag-hag yung supply chain,

asr-002150
02:34:57.120 --> 02:35:01.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: hindi maibibenta ng tama, hindi maibibenta sa tamang presyo,

asr-002151
02:35:01.840 --> 02:35:06.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: o hindi maibibenta, titatapo na lamang ang ating mga produkto.

asr-002152
02:35:06.640 --> 02:35:12.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, they have target beneficiaries of 80,000 smallholder households,

asr-002153
02:35:12.560 --> 02:35:15.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and 400,000 individual beneficiaries.

asr-002154
02:35:16.280 --> 02:35:22.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 50% of their beneficiaries are women, 30% are IMPs, and 20% kabataan.

asr-002155
02:35:22.940 --> 02:35:26.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: To reduce rural poverty and increase food security,

asr-002156
02:35:26.140 --> 02:35:29.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: while protecting and enhancing the natural ecosystems.

asr-002157
02:35:30.460 --> 02:35:34.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And of course, the clear objective is to increase income and employment,

asr-002158
02:35:35.560 --> 02:35:41.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and climate resilience of target groups in fragile upland areas,

asr-002159
02:35:41.500 --> 02:35:43.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: including women, youth, and IPs,

asr-002160
02:35:43.880 --> 02:35:46.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: through the strengthening of inclusive value chains,

asr-002161
02:35:47.400 --> 02:35:50.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: with conservation and sustainable use of natural resources.

asr-002162
02:35:50.700 --> 02:35:55.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry, it sounds very much like very similar livelihood and support services.

asr-002163
02:35:56.140 --> 02:35:56.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, is it different?

asr-002164
02:35:57.900 --> 02:35:59.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I think that was our question.

asr-002165
02:35:59.820 --> 02:36:04.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It is concentrated on two regions, namely CAR and Region 12,

asr-002166
02:36:04.600 --> 02:36:11.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and it focuses on two principal high-value crops, like coffee and camo.

asr-002167
02:36:11.600 --> 02:36:15.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, it is focused on two regions.

asr-002168
02:36:15.220 --> 02:36:18.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: This would be CAR and Region 12.

asr-002169
02:36:18.860 --> 02:36:19.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, it's CAR?

asr-002170
02:36:19.640 --> 02:36:20.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry.

asr-002171
02:36:20.900 --> 02:36:22.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Region CAR.

asr-002172
02:36:22.080 --> 02:36:25.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: CAR, okay. Cordillera and Region 12.

asr-002173
02:36:25.240 --> 02:36:25.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And Region 12.

asr-002174
02:36:26.140 --> 02:36:27.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That sucks our genes.

asr-002175
02:36:27.240 --> 02:36:27.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002176
02:36:27.820 --> 02:36:32.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And focused likewise on two principal crops,

asr-002177
02:36:33.300 --> 02:36:36.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: high-value crops, coffee and cacao.

asr-002178
02:36:36.520 --> 02:36:41.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, this is the focus, apart from the other programs.

asr-002179
02:36:42.180 --> 02:36:43.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did the House cancel it?

asr-002180
02:36:44.920 --> 02:36:48.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did the House cancel the counterpart?

asr-002192
02:36:56.140 --> 02:37:02.600
DAR Secretary Conrado M. Estrella III: Our budget utilization rate is 92%.

asr-002192-split-2
02:37:02.600 --> 02:37:23.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actually, the Secretary, who is a long-standing alumnus of the House, said it looks like the House members made a mistake in that they did not appreciate the figures in terms of absorption and utilization.

asr-002192-split-3
02:37:23.400 --> 02:37:26.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bakit akala nila hindi na-disburse?

asr-002194
02:37:26.140 --> 02:37:30.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They thought that the amounts were not being disbursed.

asr-002195
02:37:30.280 --> 02:37:31.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did that confusion occur?

asr-002196
02:37:34.220 --> 02:37:39.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because the release was delayed as in many other releases.

asr-002197
02:37:41.180 --> 02:37:43.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: July was released this year.

asr-002199
02:37:49.220 --> 02:37:54.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, it was released in July, but the actual implementation was in October.

asr-002200
02:37:54.360 --> 02:37:55.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-002201
02:37:55.060 --> 02:37:55.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But their...

asr-002202
02:37:56.140 --> 02:37:58.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The utilization rate is, in fact, 92%.

asr-002203
02:37:58.640 --> 02:37:59.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 92%.

asr-002204
02:37:59.780 --> 02:38:00.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-002205
02:38:00.820 --> 02:38:01.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

asr-002206
02:38:01.360 --> 02:38:06.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, I think the Senate was right in restoring the 600 million.

asr-002207
02:38:06.440 --> 02:38:10.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: More importantly, what is the current status of the split project?

asr-002208
02:38:10.660 --> 02:38:12.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Maraming umaasa sa split.

asr-002209
02:38:12.620 --> 02:38:17.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The project was originally scheduled two years ago.

asr-002210
02:38:17.300 --> 02:38:20.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dapat nag-close na yan, December 31, 2024, diba?

asr-002211
02:38:21.100 --> 02:38:25.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos in-extend to December 31 na naman, 2027.

asr-002212
02:38:26.140 --> 02:38:26.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Next year.

asr-002213
02:38:27.720 --> 02:38:31.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did we require a three-year extension period?

asr-002214
02:38:31.700 --> 02:38:35.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And is the DAR now on track to meet the 2027 deadline?

asr-002215
02:38:36.340 --> 02:38:38.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's already an extended deadline.

asr-002216
02:38:39.480 --> 02:38:42.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, we are full speed ahead, according to the Secretary.

asr-002217
02:38:43.060 --> 02:38:46.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The reason for the delay was the pandemic.

asr-002218
02:38:46.880 --> 02:38:48.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And because of...

asr-002219
02:38:48.260 --> 02:38:53.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, the reason for the delay primarily was because of COVID, the pandemic.

asr-002220
02:38:54.420 --> 02:38:55.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The COVID.

asr-002221
02:38:55.060 --> 02:38:55.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002222
02:38:55.280 --> 02:38:55.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-002223
02:38:56.140 --> 02:39:03.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I also understand that quite a few documents had to be redone simply because of the debt

asr-002224
02:39:03.120 --> 02:39:03.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: condonation.

asr-002225
02:39:04.340 --> 02:39:10.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, they had to reprocess it because, as it turned out, the ARBs were beneficiaries of

asr-002226
02:39:10.840 --> 02:39:11.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: the condonation as well.

asr-002227
02:39:12.180 --> 02:39:12.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That is correct.

asr-002228
02:39:13.020 --> 02:39:13.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is that correct?

asr-002229
02:39:13.980 --> 02:39:16.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And many of them had their mortgage liens already lifted.

asr-002230
02:39:17.380 --> 02:39:17.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That is correct.

asr-002231
02:39:17.960 --> 02:39:24.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, now, we are to understand that you will, in fact, meet the December 27 deadline at

asr-002232
02:39:24.620 --> 02:39:25.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: wala ng hadlang.

asr-002233
02:39:26.140 --> 02:39:27.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Wala ng extension.

asr-002234
02:39:28.440 --> 02:39:29.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Without...

asr-002235
02:39:29.240 --> 02:39:30.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: No more extension.

asr-002236
02:39:31.000 --> 02:39:32.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sir, we're probably...

asr-002237
02:39:32.800 --> 02:39:35.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, the law also gave DAR and...

asr-002238
02:39:35.620 --> 02:39:35.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry.

asr-002239
02:39:35.860 --> 02:39:37.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The farm also wants to be...

asr-002240
02:39:37.520 --> 02:39:39.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But there is a development.

asr-002241
02:39:39.500 --> 02:39:41.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The farm wishes to be included in the program.

asr-002242
02:39:43.020 --> 02:39:44.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Part of the farm.

asr-002243
02:39:44.360 --> 02:39:46.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And therefore, that might require an extension.

asr-002244
02:39:47.020 --> 02:39:48.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Only for...

asr-002245
02:39:48.340 --> 02:39:50.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But only for farm.

asr-002246
02:39:50.820 --> 02:39:52.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And no more additional funds needed.

asr-002247
02:39:52.660 --> 02:39:56.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And no more additional funds will be required.

asr-002248
02:39:56.140 --> 02:40:00.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The unused funds will be utilized.

asr-002249
02:40:00.600 --> 02:40:04.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And they're looking at 8 to 10 months for farm.

asr-002250
02:40:04.720 --> 02:40:11.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, 8 to 10 months after the 2027 December deadline, the law also gave DAR and the land

asr-002251
02:40:11.580 --> 02:40:18.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: bank 3 years to submit to Congress detailed loan records for 346 plus beneficiaries whose

asr-002252
02:40:18.900 --> 02:40:20.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: accounts would be documented.

asr-002253
02:40:20.140 --> 02:40:22.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Was that list ever submitted?

asr-002254
02:40:23.080 --> 02:40:25.220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or mag-iintay pa rin ng 2027?

asr-002255
02:40:25.580 --> 02:40:26.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or 2027?

asr-002256
02:40:26.140 --> 02:40:28.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 2027 plus 10 months as the case may be.

asr-002257
02:40:28.800 --> 02:40:30.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, the documents have been submitted.

asr-002258
02:40:31.520 --> 02:40:31.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

asr-002259
02:40:32.000 --> 02:40:33.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And they have been submitting...

asr-002260
02:40:33.200 --> 02:40:33.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We have been periodically...

asr-002261
02:40:33.920 --> 02:40:35.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero paano yung mga incomplete?

asr-002262
02:40:35.600 --> 02:40:36.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Di ba hindi nga kompleto?

asr-002263
02:40:38.240 --> 02:40:40.520
DAR Secretary Conrado M. Estrella III: Meron mga kompleto naman po lahat.

asr-002264
02:40:40.660 --> 02:40:43.160
DAR Secretary Conrado M. Estrella III: Yun lang po hindi nasubmit yung sa farm lang.

asr-002265
02:40:44.260 --> 02:40:46.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Everything was completely...

asr-002266
02:40:46.080 --> 02:40:49.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Was complete in terms of the submissions except for farm.

asr-002267
02:40:49.900 --> 02:40:50.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-002268
02:40:50.600 --> 02:40:52.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Makikibalita rin ako dun sa...

asr-002269
02:40:52.620 --> 02:40:55.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Early this year, may alleged strand grabbing of 187...

asr-002270
02:40:55.580 --> 02:41:01.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: hectares in Kapas Tarlac from ARBs.

asr-002271
02:41:01.620 --> 02:41:04.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Whatever happened to the investigation of that land grabbing incident?

asr-002272
02:41:05.880 --> 02:41:12.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Were administrative or criminal cases charged, filed against the individuals or the government

asr-002273
02:41:12.060 --> 02:41:13.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: officials involved?

asr-002274
02:41:13.620 --> 02:41:14.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: May nangyari ba dun?

asr-002275
02:41:18.840 --> 02:41:25.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, the good secretary would like to assure the good senator that if the information is not clear,

asr-002276
02:41:25.560 --> 02:41:27.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: if the information is related to them, they will look into it.

asr-002277
02:41:27.640 --> 02:41:29.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Or right now, they will now...

asr-002278
02:41:29.160 --> 02:41:34.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: No, this is already how many months running?

asr-002279
02:41:34.260 --> 02:41:35.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: This is nine months running.

asr-002280
02:41:35.820 --> 02:41:36.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pebrero pa to eh.

asr-002281
02:41:37.360 --> 02:41:44.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the secretary, at least according to the media, ordered an immediate investigation.

asr-002282
02:41:44.880 --> 02:41:45.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Anyari?

asr-002283
02:41:46.320 --> 02:41:48.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bakit ngayon palang mabalitaan?

asr-002284
02:41:50.880 --> 02:41:51.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yeah.

asr-002285
02:41:51.400 --> 02:41:54.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I wanted to know the status of the investigation.

asr-002286
02:41:55.560 --> 02:42:00.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kung may charges filed, kung who are the individuals, kung may government employees involved, kung naparusahan.

asr-002287
02:42:11.080 --> 02:42:15.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry, I came from the DAR website in February.

asr-002288
02:42:15.920 --> 02:42:17.600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi nakatutok naman ako sa DAR.

asr-002289
02:42:17.760 --> 02:42:20.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kaya nakikibalita lang ako nangyari na ron.

asr-002290
02:42:20.960 --> 02:42:21.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002291
02:42:21.480 --> 02:42:25.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The secretary has assured us that they will look into...

asr-002292
02:42:25.560 --> 02:42:27.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Do it and act on it as soon as possible.

asr-002293
02:42:27.800 --> 02:42:29.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: More importantly, could they report back?

asr-002294
02:42:29.960 --> 02:42:33.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Because there have been complaints that nothing was done.

asr-002295
02:42:36.520 --> 02:42:42.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: If you could file, if you could also provide us a copy of whatever investigation or results

asr-002296
02:42:42.080 --> 02:42:45.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: or any charges that have been filed, administrative, civil, or criminal,

asr-002297
02:42:46.140 --> 02:42:49.220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: para at least masagot naman namin na may ginawa naman yung DAR.

asr-002298
02:42:49.220 --> 02:42:51.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dahil ang sinasabi, wala raw ginawa.

asr-002299
02:42:52.280 --> 02:42:55.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The secretary issued a special order.

asr-002300
02:42:55.560 --> 02:43:01.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Order number 67, directing the regional director to look into it.

asr-002301
02:43:02.380 --> 02:43:05.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero that was February pa. Anong kinalabsan?

asr-002302
02:43:06.540 --> 02:43:06.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002303
02:43:07.160 --> 02:43:08.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yun ang gusto natin maalaman, no?

asr-002304
02:43:09.980 --> 02:43:11.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dahil, on top of that,

asr-002305
02:43:12.800 --> 02:43:16.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: oo, kung pwedeng bigyan na lang ng report dahil maraming nagsusumbong.

asr-002306
02:43:16.940 --> 02:43:18.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang problema pa kasi niyan,

asr-002307
02:43:19.300 --> 02:43:22.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: nasa kapas-tarlak na naman itong Paxilica.

asr-002308
02:43:22.940 --> 02:43:24.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At saka, may reklamo na naman.

asr-002309
02:43:24.840 --> 02:43:30.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It's intended to cover 4,000 acres originally, tapos binawasan.

asr-002310
02:43:31.540 --> 02:43:35.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And then, DAR made a statement that, in fact,

asr-002311
02:43:35.580 --> 02:43:39.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: it has not received a single application for conversion of agricultural land

asr-002312
02:43:40.400 --> 02:43:44.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: into commercial or industrial for the proposed project area.

asr-002313
02:43:45.280 --> 02:43:50.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, the question arises, we have this kapas issue of land grabbing.

asr-002314
02:43:50.660 --> 02:43:54.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ngayon naman, ang tinatanong, has there an inventory already?

asr-002315
02:43:54.840 --> 02:44:01.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: been made confirming whether any portion of the 1,619-hectare site

asr-002316
02:44:01.000 --> 02:44:04.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: covered by certain ARBs,

asr-002317
02:44:05.660 --> 02:44:06.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: awarded to ARBs?

asr-002318
02:44:07.720 --> 02:44:09.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meron na ba tayong listahan niyan?

asr-002319
02:44:09.820 --> 02:44:12.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or what's happening there?

asr-002320
02:44:13.360 --> 02:44:17.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Because there are allegations already of notices to evict.

asr-002321
02:44:17.820 --> 02:44:22.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: There are allegations of requests to sign quit claims and waivers including IPs.

asr-002322
02:44:24.840 --> 02:44:30.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, when do you plan to do that?

asr-002323
02:44:33.120 --> 02:44:34.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002324
02:44:34.220 --> 02:44:40.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The good Secretary is assuring us that before the bicam convenes, we will be updated

asr-002325
02:44:40.020 --> 02:44:41.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: regarding this particular.

asr-002326
02:44:41.800 --> 02:44:44.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or earlier. No, dapat siguro earlier.

asr-002327
02:44:45.400 --> 02:44:48.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes. But in any case,

asr-002328
02:44:48.440 --> 02:44:52.630
Senator Imee R. Marcos: have safeguards already been in place?

asr-002329
02:44:52.630 --> 02:45:00.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or can we get the assurance, um, um, can we get the assurance of our Secretary

asr-002337
02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:06.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and the entire department, that the farmers who have been awarded this land

asr-002338
02:45:06.920 --> 02:45:13.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: will not be displaced, that the land that is agricultural will not be converted

asr-002339
02:45:13.080 --> 02:45:20.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: from agricultural to whatever it is without proper consultation, restitution,

asr-002340
02:45:21.060 --> 02:45:26.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: compensation, and proof that sustainable non-agricultural livelihoods will be provided.

asr-002341
02:45:26.900 --> 02:45:37.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, the Secretary is expressing his commitment to address these concerns raised by the good Senator.

asr-002342
02:45:38.700 --> 02:45:43.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And likewise, as Chairman of the Committee on Agriculture, we assure the good Senator

asr-002343
02:45:43.240 --> 02:45:48.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: that our committee will likewise look into this and look into the safeguards

asr-002344
02:45:48.040 --> 02:45:53.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: that the good Senator has suggested so that we can address their concerns.

asr-002345
02:45:53.240 --> 02:45:56.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, thank you. And finally,

asr-002346
02:45:56.900 --> 02:46:01.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I'm a bit puzzled by this announcement.

asr-002347
02:46:02.060 --> 02:46:08.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why is DAR implementing the P28.243 billion PBBM bridges project?

asr-002348
02:46:08.780 --> 02:46:13.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What is DAR's specific mandate and expertise in bridge construction?

asr-002349
02:46:21.660 --> 02:46:26.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: According to the Secretary, they are not implementing.

asr-002350
02:46:26.900 --> 02:46:30.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They are implementing the program, the P28.243 billion bridge program, but...

asr-002351
02:46:30.740 --> 02:46:32.220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why is it under them?

asr-002352
02:46:32.220 --> 02:46:40.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They have identified the agrarian reform communities.

asr-002353
02:46:41.280 --> 02:46:44.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: All the ARCDPs are your listings?

asr-002354
02:46:44.280 --> 02:46:44.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002355
02:46:44.920 --> 02:46:49.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So how many bridges are targeted for 2027 and where will they be?

asr-002356
02:46:50.120 --> 02:46:52.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Siguro, bigyan mo na lang kami ng listahan.

asr-002358
02:46:53.280 --> 02:46:55.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, we will.

asr-002358-split-2
02:46:55.280 --> 02:46:56.220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, the draft loan...

asr-002359
02:46:56.900 --> 02:47:02.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The draft loan agreement already specifies and identifies all these ARCDPs?

asr-002360
02:47:02.160 --> 02:47:02.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002361
02:47:03.520 --> 02:47:04.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, the...

asr-002362
02:47:04.740 --> 02:47:07.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nandun sa draft loan agreement, yung...

asr-002363
02:47:07.400 --> 02:47:13.220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dun sa annexes, yung mga agrarian reform communities that will benefit from the bridge program?

asr-002364
02:47:14.220 --> 02:47:15.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What was the criteria of...

asr-002365
02:47:15.960 --> 02:47:16.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The answer is yes.

asr-002366
02:47:17.120 --> 02:47:17.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-002367
02:47:17.680 --> 02:47:26.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What was the criteria for choosing the bridges?

asr-002400
02:47:26.720 --> 02:47:32.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, they have submitted 780 locations as instructed by the...

asr-002401
02:47:32.520 --> 02:47:34.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: For 2027, lahat yan?

asr-002402
02:47:34.860 --> 02:47:37.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: No, this is for the five-year program.

asr-002403
02:47:38.080 --> 02:47:40.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, how did you choose?

asr-002404
02:47:40.740 --> 02:47:42.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: How did you select these ARCDPs?

asr-002405
02:47:43.300 --> 02:47:43.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You tell me.

asr-002406
02:47:43.960 --> 02:47:45.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What's the prioritization?

asr-002407
02:47:45.820 --> 02:47:47.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You tell me and I will tell you.

asr-002408
02:47:47.300 --> 02:47:48.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, you tell me.

asr-002409
02:47:48.000 --> 02:47:54.840
DAR Secretary Conrado M. Estrella III: The IRR, the Economic Internal Rate of Return, has been the basis of NEDA and DEPDEV to identify

asr-002410
02:47:54.840 --> 02:47:55.660
DAR Secretary Conrado M. Estrella III: and approve.

asr-002411
02:47:55.720 --> 02:47:57.960
DAR Secretary Conrado M. Estrella III: The set locations that we have submitted.

asr-002412
02:47:57.960 --> 02:48:10.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, it is a DEPDEV that identified the criteria, and based on that criteria, the DAR submitted

asr-002413
02:48:10.220 --> 02:48:14.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: the proposed number of 700?

asr-002415
02:48:16.680 --> 02:48:18.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yeah, 700.

asr-002417
02:48:21.020 --> 02:48:24.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And of the 700 plus that was recommended...

asr-002418
02:48:25.080 --> 02:48:25.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 300.

asr-002419
02:48:25.380 --> 02:48:27.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The NEDA approved 300...

asr-002420
02:48:27.640 --> 02:48:30.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: DEPDEV approved 350 total.

asr-002421
02:48:30.320 --> 02:48:30.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002422
02:48:30.780 --> 02:48:31.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

asr-002423
02:48:31.480 --> 02:48:38.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Siguro, wala kasi kaming alam tungkol dito at nakakapagtaka pag sinabing DAR, biglang may

asr-002424
02:48:38.440 --> 02:48:39.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bridges Program.

asr-002425
02:48:39.640 --> 02:48:44.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bakit hindi DPWH o di kaya yung PRDP man lang ng DA or something, ano?

asr-002426
02:48:45.200 --> 02:48:46.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kaya nagulat ng lahat.

asr-002427
02:48:46.460 --> 02:48:52.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kaya siguro, ang maaaring yung gawin, ibigay na yung listahan, yung terms of reference,

asr-002428
02:48:52.580 --> 02:48:53.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: kung ano yun.

asr-002429
02:48:53.940 --> 02:48:54.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At...

asr-002430
02:48:54.740 --> 02:49:05.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nandito kasi sa 2027 capital outlay, yung sa budget ninyo, 93.463 million for land outlay.

asr-002431
02:49:05.200 --> 02:49:09.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is this designated for right-of-way and bridge approaches?

asr-002432
02:49:10.040 --> 02:49:10.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ganun ba yun?

asr-002433
02:49:11.600 --> 02:49:12.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, that is correct.

asr-002434
02:49:12.680 --> 02:49:22.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If we may also inform the good senator that of the 28.24 billion total project cost, because

asr-002435
02:49:22.380 --> 02:49:24.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: this is a official development aid.

asr-002436
02:49:24.740 --> 02:49:24.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Right.

asr-002437
02:49:25.540 --> 02:49:31.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The government counterpart for 2027 is 1.4 billion.

asr-002438
02:49:33.340 --> 02:49:34.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: For that entity?

asr-002439
02:49:34.420 --> 02:49:34.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-002440
02:49:34.800 --> 02:49:46.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, and that's why it is the DAR that is the institution that is now working in partnership

asr-002441
02:49:46.600 --> 02:49:50.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: with the host LGUs and the DPWH.

asr-002442
02:49:51.200 --> 02:49:51.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oh, I see.

asr-002443
02:49:52.180 --> 02:49:53.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It is the DAR because...

asr-002444
02:49:54.740 --> 02:50:02.600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry.

asr-002445
02:50:03.120 --> 02:50:03.280
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Yeah.

asr-002446
02:50:03.660 --> 02:50:11.600
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, if I may, to assist our sponsor, because we have that program in Bukidnon.

asr-002447
02:50:11.600 --> 02:50:15.980
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Many of our grand reform communities are actually funded their roads.

asr-002448
02:50:16.800 --> 02:50:21.860
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And mind you, they're very good roads and bridges going to the ARCs, the grand reform

asr-002449
02:50:21.860 --> 02:50:24.700
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: communities, that were funded by loan programs from DAR.

asr-002450
02:50:24.740 --> 02:50:26.740
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Apparently, DAR has a...

asr-002451
02:50:27.260 --> 02:50:34.420
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: There are governments and the financial institutions that look towards these programs for grand

asr-002452
02:50:34.420 --> 02:50:34.780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: reform.

asr-002453
02:50:34.960 --> 02:50:41.180
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So, they top that and they do a better job actually identifying the areas.

asr-002454
02:50:41.520 --> 02:50:42.180
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Hindi siya ghost.

asr-002455
02:50:42.860 --> 02:50:44.420
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Grand reform communities talaga siya.

asr-002456
02:50:44.540 --> 02:50:47.980
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Because, ang nag-recommend is ARC, the communities itself.

asr-002457
02:50:48.340 --> 02:50:53.180
